  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures a compact, intimate performance by The Mountain Goats at Easy Street Records in Seattle on August 10, 2026 [1]. Taking place just days after a larger outdoor event near Woodland Park Zoo, the band delivered a shorter, sweatier set inside the packed record store [1]. The lineup featured John Darnielle, Matt Douglas, and Jon Wurster, who arranged themselves in a horizontal line rather than placing the drummer in the back, creating an up-close experience for the crowd that stretched around the block [1]. Entry required pre-ordering a record, which attendees picked up at the front desk before the show began on time [1]. The setlist includes \"Opening Crowd Noise,\" the only archived performance of that track, and \"Crying on Eddie Nash's Grave,\" one of six archived performances [1][2]. The band also played \"Cadaver Sniffing Dog,\" their first time performing it in 77 archived shows, and \"Song for Layne Staley,\" another rare entry with six archived performances [1][2]. A cover of The Polecats' \"Make a Circuit With Me\" appears as the only archived performance of that song [1][2]. The set concludes with \"This Year,\" following tracks like \"No Children\" and \"Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds\" [1][2]. This is the 461st of 467 archived shows for the performer, following a June 2026 date at Fitzgerald's [2]. The recording documents the full 13-song set in 50 minutes [1].",
